<title>USA: Fire hits PSE&amp;G substation in New Jersey.</title>
<headline>Fire hits PSE&amp;G substation in New Jersey.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>A fire broke out at a Public Service Electric &amp; Gas Co (PSE&amp;G) power substation in Elizabeth, N.J., early Friday, local radio reported.</p>
<p>The fire was reported to be affecting power to the nearby Newark International Airport but the extent of damage to the substation was not immediately known.</p>
<p>Traffic reporters overhead in a helicopter said the flames had engulfed one corner of the substation. Firefighters were standing by but had not yet begun to douse the flames, according to the radio report.</p>
<p>(New York Power Desk 212-859-1621)</p>
